---
import SiteFooter from "../../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../../../styles/global.css";

const title = "Privacy Policy — Make Your Own Label Maker";
const description = "Privacy policy for the Make Your Own Label Maker mobile app.";
const updated = "9 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
	<SiteHeader currentPath={Astro.url.pathname} />
	<main id="main" class="subpage-main legal-main">
		<nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
			<a href="/apps/">Apps</a>
			<span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
			<a href="/apps/make-your-own-label-maker/">Make Your Own Label Maker</a>
			<span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
			<span aria-current="page">Privacy policy</span>
		</nav>

		<section class="legal-hero" aria-labelledby="policy-heading">
			<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
			<h1 id="policy-heading">Privacy policy</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				This policy explains how Make Your Own Label Maker handles information when you use
				the mobile app.
			</p>
			<p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
		</section>

		<div class="legal-layout">
			<aside class="legal-summary" aria-labelledby="summary-heading">
				<h2 id="summary-heading">The short version</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>No account is required.</li>
					<li>Your label projects are stored on your device.</li>
					<li>We do not use advertising or analytics services.</li>
					<li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
				</ul>
			</aside>

			<article class="legal-content">
				<section>
					<h2>1. Who this policy covers</h2>
					<p>
						This privacy policy applies to the Make Your Own Label Maker mobile application,
						operated by LWilsonDev ("we", "us" or "our"). It does not cover third-party
						websites or services that you choose to open from the app.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>2. Information the app handles</h2>
					<h3>Photos and camera images</h3>
					<p>
						If you choose to add an image, the app asks for camera or photo-library access. It
						only accesses a photo when you take or select one. The chosen image is copied into
						the app's private storage on your device so it can be used in your label.
					</p>

					<h3>Label projects</h3>
					<p>
						Text, images, stickers, layout choices, project names and project dates are saved
						locally in the app's private storage. We do not receive these projects and the app
						does not upload them to a server operated by us.
					</p>

					<h3>Printing</h3>
					<p>
						When you choose to print, the app creates a printable image and passes it to your
						device's print service. Any printer or print service you select may process that
						content under its own privacy terms. We do not receive a copy.
					</p>

					<h3>Web image search</h3>
					<p>
						The optional web-search feature opens a Google Images search in your browser. Your
						search terms and normal browser or device information are sent directly to Google,
						not to us. Google's handling of that information is governed by its own privacy
						policy. You decide whether to download an image and add it from your photo library.
					</p>

					<h3>Technical and usage data</h3>
					<p>
						The current version of the app does not use analytics, advertising or crash-reporting
						services and does not collect advertising identifiers, precise location, contacts or
						account credentials. Apple, Google, your device provider and the app store may process
						download, diagnostic or transaction information independently under their own terms.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>3. Device permissions</h2>
					<div class="permission-grid">
						<div>
							<strong>Camera</strong>
							<span>Used only when you choose to take a photo for a label.</span>
						</div>
						<div>
							<strong>Photo library</strong>
							<span>Used only when you choose an existing image for a label.</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>
						You can refuse or withdraw these permissions in your device settings. The app will
						still work, but features that need the relevant permission will be unavailable.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>4. How information is used</h2>
					<p>The app uses information you provide only to:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>create, edit, save and preview your label projects;</li>
						<li>prepare the labels you choose to print; and</li>
						<li>open a web image search when you request one.</li>
					</ul>
					<p>We do not use your content for advertising, profiling or training AI models.</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>5. Sharing and disclosure</h2>
					<p>
						We do not sell, rent or share your label projects or personal information with third
						parties because we do not receive them. Information leaves the app only when you
						direct it to—for example, by opening Google Images, using your device's print service
						or interacting with an app store. Those third parties act under their own terms.
					</p>
					<p>
						We may disclose information if required by law, but we can only disclose information
						that we actually hold.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>6. Storage, retention and deletion</h2>
					<p>
						Label projects and imported images remain on your device until you delete the project
						or uninstall the app. Your operating system may include app data in a device backup;
						backup retention is controlled by your device or backup provider. Because the app has
						no user accounts and we do not hold your projects on our servers, there is no separate
						online account or cloud record for us to delete.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>7. Security</h2>
					<p>
						Keeping projects in the app's private on-device storage limits their exposure. You
						should keep your device software up to date and use a screen lock. No storage method is
						completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>8. Children</h2>
					<p>
						The app is intended to be used by adults and does not knowingly collect personal
						information from children. A child should use the app only with a parent or guardian's
						supervision. If you believe a child has sent information to us, please contact us.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>9. Your choices and rights</h2>
					<p>
						You can choose which photos to add, remove saved projects, revoke camera or photo
						permissions, and uninstall the app to remove its local data. Depending on where you
						live, you may also have legal rights concerning personal information. As we do not
						collect your app content or operate user accounts, we will normally have no app data
						linked to you, but you can contact us with any privacy question.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>10. International data transfers</h2>
					<p>
						We do not transfer your label projects to our servers in any country. Third-party
						services you choose to use may process information internationally under their own
						privacy policies.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
					<p>
						We may update this policy when the app or legal requirements change. We will post the
						revised policy on this page and change the date above. Material changes will be
						communicated in the app where appropriate.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>12. Contact</h2>
					<p>
						For privacy questions or requests, email
						<a href="mailto:lwilsondev2@gmail.com">lwilsondev2@gmail.com</a>.
					</p>
					<p>
						LWilsonDev is the trading name used by Lucy Wilson, the data controller responsible
						for the app.
					</p>
				</section>
			</article>
		</div>
	</main>
	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
